{
  "id": "ep088",
  "duration": 52.929,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.129,
      "text": "A 1,000-foot city killer slipped right past Earth without anyone noticing.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA21259 - Celestial Object 2016 WF9, a NEOWISE Discovery (Artist Concept).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA21259_-_Celestial_Object_2016_WF9,_a_NEOWISE_Discovery_(Artist_Concept).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.3,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 5.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.129,
      "end": 13.724,
      "text": "On March 31, 1989, astronomers Henry Holt and Norman Thomas spotted a faint streak at Palomar Observatory.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "California - Palomar Observator through Parker Dam - NARA - 23934813.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:California_-_Palomar_Observator_through_Parker_Dam_-_NARA_-_23934813.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.133,
          "end": 8.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.867,
          "end": 13.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.724,
      "end": 18.319,
      "text": "When they calculated its orbit, the data revealed something terrifying.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "2001 SG286 orbit.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2001_SG286_orbit.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.733,
          "end": 18.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.319,
      "end": 24.814,
      "text": "Nine days earlier, in late March 1989, this massive rock had swept past our planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.333,
          "end": 24.8,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.814,
      "end": 33.959,
      "text": "Designated 4581 [Asclepius](/\u00e6zkl\u02c8ip\u02c8i\u02cc\u028cs/), it missed us by 425,000 miles, roughly twice the distance to the Moon.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Earth Moon Nereid.png",
        "credit": "IapetusCallistus",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earth_Moon_Nereid.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.8,
          "end": 29.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 33.967,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.959,
      "end": 40.979,
      "text": "Had it struck an ocean, calculations showed it would unleash the power of a 600-megaton atomic explosion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.967,
          "end": 40.967,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.979,
      "end": 47.729,
      "text": "The shock of missing this close call forced governments to establish modern planetary defense networks.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dart-poster3.jpg",
        "credit": "Credits: NASA/Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Lab",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dart-poster3.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.967,
          "end": 45.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 45.367,
          "end": 47.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.729,
      "end": 52.579,
      "text": "It was a chilling reminder of how easily a massive asteroid can sneak past us.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA21259 - Celestial Object 2016 WF9, a NEOWISE Discovery (Artist Concept).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA21259_-_Celestial_Object_2016_WF9,_a_NEOWISE_Discovery_(Artist_Concept).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.733,
          "end": 52.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
